#### 1. Constructors
A constructor is a member function of a class that is mainly used to initialise objects of the class. It has the same name as the class, is called automatically at the time of object creation, and has no return type.

Syntax:

```cpp
class Student {
    int x1, x2;
public:
    Student() {
        x1 = 1;
        x2 = 2;
    }
};
```

Types:

- Default
- Parameterized
- Copy

#### 2. Destructor
A destructor is another type of member function, responsible for destroying the object by freeing the space occupied by it after it is no longer needed. It is called automatically when the object goes out of scope.

Syntax:

```cpp
~Student() { }
```

