Let `a` and `b` be the two integers to swap.

i) Using the reference operator (call by **reference**, call as `Swap_reference(a, b)`):

```cpp
void Swap_reference(int &a, int &b)
{
    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp;
}
```

ii) Using pointers (call by **reference**, call as `swap_pointer(&a, &b)`):

```cpp
void swap_pointer(int *a, int *b)
{
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}
```

iii) Using ordinary variables (call by **value**, call as `swap_ordinary(a, b)`; the original values are not swapped):

```cpp
void swap_ordinary(int a, int b)
{
    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp;
}
```

